{{!-- The site's own furniture, in the left gutter.

The blocks and their order are the blog engine's: menu, featured, tags. Each is skipped when
it has nothing to say, so a new blog shows a short rail rather than three empty headings.

TWO of the engine's five blocks are not here.
  · Categories. Ghost has tags and nothing else, and inventing a taxonomy in a theme would
    put content structure in the layer that is supposed to be about looks. The engine's TAG
    block is the one that ships, lowercased and without counts, because that is what the
    engine does with a tag.
  · Archive. A year is a URL, and Ghost has no date route to point one at without a
    `routes.yaml` the owner installs by hand — a site file, not something a theme can carry.
    docs/gaps.md has the file and what it costs.

An Authors block stands where Categories did, and only on a blog that has more than one:
it is the nearest thing Ghost has to a second way through the archive. --}}
<aside class="rail" aria-label="Site">
<div class="rail-inner">

{{navigation}}

{{#get "posts" filter="featured:true" limit="5"}}
    {{#if posts}}
    <div>
        <h2>Featured</h2>
        <ul style="--count-w:1ch">
            {{#foreach posts}}<li><a class="rail-row link-accent t-small" href="{{url}}"><span>{{title}}</span></a></li>{{/foreach}}
        </ul>
    </div>
    {{/if}}
{{/get}}

{{#get "authors" limit="8" include="count.posts"}}
    {{!-- A second entry is the test: on a one-author blog this block is a heading over the
    owner's own name, which tells a reader nothing they did not know from the footer. --}}
    {{#if authors.[1]}}
    <div>
        <h2>Authors</h2>
        <div class="rail-tags">
            {{#foreach authors}}<a class="link-accent t-small" href="{{url}}">{{name}}<span class="term-count">{{count.posts}}</span></a>{{/foreach}}
        </div>
    </div>
    {{/if}}
{{/get}}

{{#get "tags" limit="40" order="count.posts desc" include="count.posts" filter="visibility:public"}}
    {{#if tags}}
    <div>
        <h2>Tags</h2>
        {{!-- No counts, and lowercased by the sheet: a tag is a word, and thirty words each
        carrying a number is a table rather than a cloud. --}}
        <div class="rail-tags lower">
            {{#foreach tags}}<a class="link-accent t-small" href="{{url}}">{{name}}</a>{{/foreach}}
        </div>
    </div>
    {{/if}}
{{/get}}

</div>
</aside>
